amed + Exotics!F83') #(description 'Enemies you kill drop a trophy on death. Collecting trophies provides both a short and long term buff, the first of which scales with the number of core attributes equipped and lasts 10s. /  / Red Core - 5% Weapon Damage / Blue Core - 10% Bonus Armor / Yellow Core - 5% Skill Effciency /  / For every trophy collected gain an additional +1% weapon damage, +1% skill efficiency and +0.1% armor regeneration for 300s /  / Maximum 30 stacks' 'Gear Named + Exotics!G83') #(core 'Weapon damage / 1.5% - 15%' 'Gear Named + Exotics!H83') #(minor1 'Armour / 16,594 - 170,000' 'Gear Named + Exotics!I83') #(minor2 '>+1< / Skill tier' 'Gear Named + Exotics!J83') #(minor3 'Mod Slot' 'Gear Named + Exotics!K83') #(acquisition '- Season 3 track /  / -- Target loot / -- Exotic Caches' 'Gear Named + Exotics!M83') #(flavour '"I took from those who watched, hunted, and collected, until only tgheir shadows remained. Now my watch has ended, so yours may begin." /  / - Inscription by an unknown author /  /  / - The name "Memento" is a reference to  the fact that Hunters keep watches of Agents they have killed as sick mementos.  / - The axes on the backpack are Hunter axes. These Crash Axes, the same ones found in planes. While usually used for breaching and rescue,  / Hunters use these axes to melee Agents who get too close. / - +5% Skill Efficiency grants +5% of every yellow minor attribute (skill haste, status effects, skill health...). +1% Skill Efficiency grants +1%. / - Memento is suspiciously similar to Prism Gloves, a joke exotic posted by Azurmen32 to the Division 2 subreddit. This is part of a running gag about  / rainbow roll items being good.' 'Gear Named + Exotics!N83'))) #('NinjaBike Messenger Backpack' 'Backpack' exotic nil #(#(slot 'Backpack' 'Gear Named + Exotics!A79') #(name 'NinjaBike  / Messenger Backpack' 'Gear Named + Exotics!D86') #(talent 'Resourceful' 'Gear Named + Exotics!F85') #(description '/ Slots in with any equipped Gear Set and/